midterm environment", "Independent pollsters (Quinnipiac, Siena) show Hochul ahead by 9-19 points; published averages cluster near 11-13", "Prediction markets price Hochul at 96-98% and most raters call the race Solid or Safe D", "Late tightening - Trump campaigning in Syracuse and narrower GOP-sponsored polls - leaves Blakeman a long but nonzero path"], "rationale": "New York's Democratic lean, Hochul's incumbency and a friendly environment stack the deck, and the strongest independent pollsters keep her ahead by high single to double digits. Markets and most raters treat this as a Solid Democratic hold, with only modest tightening signals in the final month.", "watch": "If Trump's late campaigning moves the race toward the single-digit margins shown in Republican-sponsored surveys, the rating could slip toward Likely D.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Kathy Hochul (D) is running."]}, "overview": "New York's governor race pairs incumbent Democrat Kathy Hochul against Republican Bruce Blakeman in a state that leans Democratic by eight points. Polling throughout the year has kept Hochul in front, with the most recent Quinnipiac and Siena surveys showing leads of nine to nineteen points. Fundraising is roughly comparable, with Hochul raising about $16.6 million to Blakeman's $13.4 million, though the incumbent holds more cash entering the final month.\n\nAnalysts across the spectrum rate the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets put Hochul's win chances around 96 to 98 percent. Signs of a closer contest, including Trump's planned Syracuse rally, both candidates campaigning in Erie County, and narrower margins in Republican-sponsored polls, suggest Blakeman can keep it competitive. But his sparse policy detail and the state's blue tilt leave him a clear underdog.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9859, "margin": 12.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9776, "margin": 12